<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαξαίνω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έξᾱνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Gp.</u>
					2.6.42
				</span></i>
			, but inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ξῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					578
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εξαμμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					8.415
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εξασμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					5.106
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cael.</u>
				571.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.61
			</span></i>:—<i>card, shred,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				578
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθῆτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					11.14.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεῦρον εἰς ἶνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aphr.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					2.52
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				7.26.170
			</span></i>; of flesh, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.77
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				88
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of alum, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
			</span></i> l.c., <i>to be dispersed, broken up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simp.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμην,</span> of the wind, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				3.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. θάλασσαν πτερύγεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					5.306
				</span></i>
			; as a punishment, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					131
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ Ῥωμαίων ἐκτριβέντες
				διεξάνθησαν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				130
			</span></i>.</div>
